U\", \"Athletico\" | accents + state/country codes + parenthetical |\n| BR-Football | \"Sao Paulo\", \"Atletico Mineiro\", \"Botafogo RJ\", \"EC Bahia\", \"Vasco Da Gama RJ\", \"Nautico Capibaribe\", \"Guarani SP\" | no accents, full suffixes, club prefixes |\n| novo_campeonato | \"São Paulo\", \"Athletico-PR\", \"Atlético-MG\", \"Vasco\", \"Botafogo-RJ\" | accents + suffixes |\n\nCanonical mapping needed. Let me build an alias table mapping ASCII-lowercase-normalized keys to canonical display names:\n\n- corinthians → \"Corinthians\"\n- corinthians paulista, sport club corinthians paulista → \"Corinthians\"\n- flamengo → \"Flamengo\"\n- fluminense → \"Fluminense\"\n- palmeiras → \"Palmeiras\"\n- santos → \"Santos\"\n- sao paulo → \"São Paulo\"\n- gremio → \"Grêmio\"\n- internacional → \"Internacional\"\n- vasco / vasco da gama → \"Vasco da Gama\"\n- botafogo / botafogo rj → \"Botafogo\"\n- atletico mineiro / atletico-mg / atletico mg / clube atletico mineiro / atletico → hmm \"Atletico\" alone in Libertadores means Athletico Paranaense? In Libertadores file \"Athletico\" appears (2019+ seasons, they rebranded as \"Athletico\"). And \"Atlético-MG\" separately. So bare \"Athletico\" → \"Athletico Paranaense\"? In the Libertadores dataset, \"Athletico\" with capital A-t-h-l-e-t-i-c-o (h after t) is the Paranaense rebrand. And \"Atletico\" (no h)... risk. I'll map \"athletico\" → \"Athletico Paranaense\", \"atletico pr\"/\"atletico-paranaense\"/\"athletico paranaense\"/\"ca paranaense\" → \"Athletico Paranaense\", \"atletico mg\"/\"atletico mineiro\" → \"Atlético Mineiro\", \"atletico go\"/\"atletico goianiense\" → \"Atlético Goianiense\".\n- \"atletico\" bare → ambiguous; in datasets: Brasileirao uses \"Atletico-MG\"/\"Atletico-PR\"/\"Atletico-GO\" always suffixed. Cup uses \"Atlético - MG\" etc. suffixed. BR-Football uses \"Atletico Mineiro\"/\"Atletico Goianiense\". Libertadores: \"Atlético-MG\" and \"Athletico\". So bare \"Atletico\" rarely occurs; if it does, keep as-is.\n- sport / sport recife → \"Sport Recife\"\n- bahia / ec bahia → \"Bahia\"\n- cruzeiro → \"Cruzeiro\"\n- coritiba → \"Coritiba\"\n- chapecoense → \"Chapecoense\"\n- goias → \"Goiás\"\n- ponte preta → \"Ponte Preta\"\n- vitoria / ec vitoria → \"Vitória\"\n- ceara → \"Ceará\"\n- figueirense → \"Figueirense\"\n- avai → \"Avaí\"\n- america mg / america-mg / america mineiro → \"América Mineiro\"\n- america rn → \"América-RN\"\n- america (bare) → \"América\" hmm, keep bare.\n- fortaleza / fortaleza esporte clube → \"Fortaleza\"\n- red bull bragantino / bragantino → \"Bragantino\"\n- portuguesa → \"Portuguesa\"\n- nautico / nautico capibaribe / naútico → \"Náutico\"\n- criciuma / criciúma → \"Criciúma\"\n- cuiaba / cuiabá → \"Cuiabá\"\n- juventude / ec juventude → \"Juventude\"\n- joinville → \"Joinville\"\n- santa cruz → \"Santa Cruz\"\n- parana / paraná / paraná clube → \"Paraná\"\n- csa / csa al → \"CSA\"\n- abc → \"ABC\"\n- sampaio correa / sampaio corrêa → \"Sampaio Corrêa\"\n- paysandu → \"Paysandu\"\n- londrina → \"Londrina\"\n- guarani / guarani sp → \"Guarani\"\n- vila nova → \"Vila Nova\"\n- crb → \"CRB\"\n- brasil de pelotas → \"Brasil de Pelotas\"\n- oeste → \"Oeste\"\n- brasiliense → \"Brasiliense\"\n- sao caetano → \"São Caetano\"\n- ipatinga → \"Ipatinga\"\n- santo andre → \"Santo André\"\n- barueri / gremio barueri → \"Grêmio Barueri\"? novo has \"Barueri\" and \"Grêmio Prudente\". Keep \"Barueri\" → \"Barueri\"; \"Gremio Prudente\" → \"Grêmio Prudente\".\n- boavista sport club (antigo esporte clube barreira) - rj → \"Boavista\"\n- Foreign (Libertadores): strip country suffix/codes: \"Nacional (URU)\", \"Nacional-URU\" → \"Nacional (Uruguay)\"? Keep simple: \"Nacional\" — but that collides with \"Nacional - AM\" (Brazilian club from Manaus, in Copa do Brasil)! Hmm. \"Nacional-URU\" → key \"nacional uru\"; \"Nacional (URU)\" → same key after stripping parens: \"nacional\". Conflict with \"Nacional - AM\" → \"nacional\". Two different clubs. To be safe, keep country qualifiers: for non-Brazilian teams, canonical = cleaned name + country in parens if country code was present: \"Nacional (URU)\" and \"Nacional-URU\" → same canonical \"Nacional (URU)\". \"Nacional - AM\" → Brazilian state code → \"Nacional-AM\"? Hmm.\n\nSimplest robust rule:\n- Strip parenthetical \"(antigo ...)\" commentary but keep \"(URU)\" country codes → convert trailing \"-URU\"/\"-EQU\"/\"-PAR\" or parenthetical to a country qualifier.\n- For Brazilian state codes (the UF list), strip them entirely (they're part of naming convention, not disambiguators mostly... except América-MG vs América-RN and Nacional-AM). For those, if the base name is ambiguous (\"América\", \"Nacional\", \"Atlético\", \"Athletico\"), keep the qualifier: \"América-MG\", \"América-RN\", \"Nacional-AM\". If base maps to a known alias (atletico-mg → Atlético Mineiro etc.), use canonical.\n\nDesign: `canonical_team(raw)`:\n1. Trim. Extract trailing country code: patterns `- URU`, `-URU`, `(URU)`, `- EQU`, ` (antigo ...)` removal.\n2. Extract trailing state code for known UF list: SP, RJ, MG, RS, PR, PE, BA, SC, GO, CE, MT, AL, RN, PA, MA, AM, MS, PI, DF, ES, PB, SE, AC, AP, RR, RO, TO — via regex `(?:\\s*-\\s*|\\s+)([A-Z]{2})$` (uppercase only, so \"Vasco Da Gama RJ\" → \"RJ\" stripped; \"Botafogo RJ\" → \"Botafogo\").\n3. Base = remainder, cleaned of parentheticals like \"(antigo Esporte Clube Barreira)\".\n4. key = ascii-fold(base).lower(), collapse non-alnum to space, strip.\n5. Look up alias dict → canonical display. Special handling: if base key in {\"america\", \"nacional\", \"atletico\", \"athletico\", \"atletico nacional\", \"barcelona\"} and a qualifier was present → qualified canonical (e.g. \"América-MG\", \"Nacional (URU)\").\n6. Else canonical = base with original accents preserved (the cleaned string), minus club prefixes \"EC \", \"SC \", \"Esporte Clube \", \"Sport Club \", \"Clube \" maybe. Hmm — \"EC Bahia\" → \"Bahia\" via alias \"ec bahia\". \"Nautico 