{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788205364639,"sessionID":"ses_fa6ae4622ffeRIXSVkVPYYmujp","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_d35419a521584931bc4036be","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Brazilian Soccer MCP Server - dependencies\nmcp>=2.1.1\npytest>=9.0\npytest-bdd>=8.1\npytest-cov>=7.0\n","filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/requirements.txt"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/requirements.txt","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"requirements.txt","time":{"start":1788205364630,"end":1788205364637}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Data quirks confirmed:\n- Libertadores has \"NA\" season and \"-\" goals for some rows → handle.\n- BR-Football goals are float strings.\n- BR-Football spans 2014-2023 → overlaps with Brasileirao_Matches (Serie A 2014-2021), Cup (2014-2021), and novo (Serie A 2014-2019).\n\nDedupe strategy: unify by (competition_key, date, home_key, away_key). Order of loading: primary match files first (Brasileirao_Matches, Brazilian_Cup, Libertadores), then extended BR-Football (merge extra stats into existing dups), then novo_campeonato (merge arena). Extended Series B/C matches are new (not in other files) so they stay as their own competition entries.\n\nWait — one problem: BR-Football team names are unaccented (\"Sao Paulo\", \"Gremio\") — canonicalization maps via alias table so keys match ✓. But extended file team names for foreign/smaller clubs may differ subtly (e.g. \"Botafogo RJ\" → \"Botafogo\" ✓ aliased).\n\nCompetition canonical mapping for BR-Football tournaments: \"Serie A\" → \"Brasileirão Série A\", \"Serie B\" → \"Brasileirão Série B\", \"Serie C\" → \"Brasileirão Série C\", \"Copa do Brasil\" → \"Copa do Brasil\".\n\nDedupe stats to expect: I'll compute after implementation and pin in tests.\n\nSeason for extended matches: derive from date (year).\n\nNow, before writing code — the season of deduped extended matches: BR-Football has no season column; derive year from date. For matches on New Year's Eve of a season spanning... fine, use year.\n\nAlso HT result columns: ht_result/at_result are WON/LOST/DRAW from home perspective presumably.\n\nLet me now write all the code. Structure:\n\n```\npyproject.toml\nrequirements.txt\nbrazilian_soccer_mcp/__init__.py\nbrazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\nbrazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\nbrazilian_soccer_mcp/knowledge_graph.py\nbrazilian_soccer_mcp/queries.py\nbrazilian_soccer_mcp/server.py\nbrazilian_soccer_mcp/__main__.py\nfeatures/match_queries.feature\nfeatures/team_queries.feature\nfeatures/player_queries.feature\nfeatures/competition_queries.feature\nfeatures/statistical_analysis.feature\ntests/conftest.py\ntests/steps/test_match_queries.py\ntests/steps/test_team_queries.py\ntests/steps/test_player_queries.py\ntests/steps/test_competition_queries.py\ntests/steps/test_statistical_analysis.py\ntests/test_normalize.py\ntests/test_data_loader.py\ntests/test_knowledge_graph.py\ntests/test_server_tools.py\nREADME.md (update)\n```\n\nNote pytest-bdd: scenarios path relative to the test file. conftest provides fixtures.\n\nLet me write normalize.py first.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0595875910013nKiKgQ0xMU717","sessionID":"ses_fa6ae4622ffeRIXSVkVPYYmujp","messageID":"msg_059582101001c9HqyMGvlhET1d"}}
