{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788205755880,"sessionID":"ses_fa6ae4622ffeRIXSVkVPYYmujp","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_63d7a37185d147468ebaedcd","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/queries.py","newString":"        club_key = key_team(resolved)\n        players = [\n            p for p in self.data.players\n            if p.club and p.club_key and (\n                p.club_key == club_key or club_key in p.club_key or p.club_key in club_key\n            )\n        ]","oldString":"        club_key = key_team(resolved)\n        players = [\n            p for p in self.data.players\n            if p.club_key == club_key or club_key in p.club_key or p.club_key in club_key\n        ]"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/queries.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/queries.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/queries.py\n@@ -357,9 +357,11 @@\n \n club_key = key_team(resolved)\n players = [\n     p for p in self.data.players\n-    if p.club_key == club_key or club_key in p.club_key or p.club_key in club_key\n+    if p.club and p.club_key and (\n+        p.club_key == club_key or club_key in p.club_key or p.club_key in club_key\n+    )\n ]\n players.sort(key=lambda p: (-(p.overall or 0), p.name))\n players_view = [p.as_dict() for p in players[:15]]\n \n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/queries.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/queries.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/queries.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/queries.py\n@@ -357,9 +357,11 @@\n \n club_key = key_team(resolved)\n players = [\n     p for p in self.data.players\n-    if p.club_key == club_key or club_key in p.club_key or p.club_key in club_key\n+    if p.club and p.club_key and (\n+        p.club_key == club_key or club_key in p.club_key or p.club_key in club_key\n+    )\n ]\n players.sort(key=lambda p: (-(p.overall or 0), p.name))\n players_view = [p.as_dict() for p in players[:15]]\n \n","additions":3,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer_mcp/queries.py","time":{"start":1788205755877,"end":1788205755879}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"There's a bug in `team_overview`: the ternary in `summary = (...) if seasons else ...` — I wrote:\n\n```python\nsummary = (\n    f\"...\"\n    if seasons else\n    f\"...\"\n)\n```\n\nLet me check the syntax — I wrote:\n```python\n        summary = (\n            f\"{resolved} overview: ...\"\n            f\"Seasons covered: {seasons[0]}-{seasons[-1]}.\" if seasons else\n            f\"{resolved} overview: {record['played']} matches in dataset.\"\n        )\n```\nThe implicit string concat with the conditional — `(A B if seasons else C)` parses as `(A B) if seasons else C`? Actually implicit concatenation binds tighter than conditional: `f\"...\" f\"...\" if seasons else f\"...\"` → `(f\"...\" f\"...\") if seasons else f\"...\"`. That works syntactically. OK but readability is poor; fine for now.\n\nAlso in `team_overview`, player matching: `p.club_key == club_key or club_key in p.club_key or p.club_key in club_key` — could over-match (e.g. \"Sport Recife\" vs \"Sporting CP\"? key \"sporting cp\" contains \"sport\"? No: `p.club_key in club_key` — \"sporting cp\" in \"sport recife\"? No. \"sport\" key is \"sport recife\". OK reasonable.\n\nWait, club_key for empty club \"\" — `key_team(\"\")` returns \"\" — and `\"\" in club_key` is True for any club_key! Players with empty club would match every team. Guard: `if p.club and (...)`. Need to fix.\n\nAlso `_record` win_rate when no matches — None; summary prints \"Win rate None%\". Handle: if record['played'] == 0, different summary. Let me fix these issues now.\n\nAlso in `search_matches` — when team_r is None but opponent given, pool = matches_for_team(opponent) ✓.\n\nAlso `head_to_head` uses pool[-10:][::-1] for recent ✓.\n\nFix the two issues in queries.py.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0595e6de1001Gq0GhXUJHi4qUk","sessionID":"ses_fa6ae4622ffeRIXSVkVPYYmujp","messageID":"msg_0595e2021001EDGoL04Wkrd4Uz"}}
