{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788206110177,"sessionID":"ses_fa6ae4622ffeRIXSVkVPYYmujp","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_e2f47e026ffe4773a9180814","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py","newString":"    base, state, country = _split_qualifiers(raw_name)\n    if not base:\n        return raw_name.strip()\n    key = normalize_key(base)\n\n    # 1) Base name resolves directly (\"Sao Paulo\", \"EC Bahia\").\n    if key in TEAM_ALIASES:\n        return TEAM_ALIASES[key]\n    # 2) Base + state qualifier resolves (\"Atletico\" + \"PR\" -> \"Athletico Paranaense\").\n    if state:\n        combo = f\"{key} {state.lower()}\"\n        if combo in TEAM_ALIASES:\n            return TEAM_ALIASES[combo]\n    # 3) Ambiguous bases must keep a geographic qualifier to stay distinct.\n    if key in AMBIGUOUS_BASES:\n        if state:\n            return f\"{AMBIGUOUS_BASES[key]}-{state}\"\n        if country:\n            return f\"{AMBIGUOUS_BASES[key]} ({country})\"\n    if country:\n        return f\"{base} ({country})\"\n    return base","oldString":"    base, state, country = _split_qualifiers(raw_name)\n    if not base:\n        return raw_name.strip()\n    key = normalize_key(base)\n\n    if key in TEAM_ALIASES:\n        return TEAM_ALIASES[key]\n    if key in AMBIGUOUS_BASES:\n        if state:\n            return f\"{AMBIGUOUS_BASES[key]}-{state}\"\n        if country:\n            return f\"{AMBIGUOUS_BASES[key]} ({country})\"\n    if country:\n        return f\"{base} ({country})\"\n    return base"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n@@ -292,10 +292,17 @@\n if not base:\n     return raw_name.strip()\n key = normalize_key(base)\n \n+# 1) Base name resolves directly (\"Sao Paulo\", \"EC Bahia\").\n if key in TEAM_ALIASES:\n     return TEAM_ALIASES[key]\n+# 2) Base + state qualifier resolves (\"Atletico\" + \"PR\" -> \"Athletico Paranaense\").\n+if state:\n+    combo = f\"{key} {state.lower()}\"\n+    if combo in TEAM_ALIASES:\n+        return TEAM_ALIASES[combo]\n+# 3) Ambiguous bases must keep a geographic qualifier to stay distinct.\n if key in AMBIGUOUS_BASES:\n     if state:\n         return f\"{AMBIGUOUS_BASES[key]}-{state}\"\n     if country:\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n@@ -292,10 +292,17 @@\n if not base:\n     return raw_name.strip()\n key = normalize_key(base)\n \n+# 1) Base name resolves directly (\"Sao Paulo\", \"EC Bahia\").\n if key in TEAM_ALIASES:\n     return TEAM_ALIASES[key]\n+# 2) Base + state qualifier resolves (\"Atletico\" + \"PR\" -> \"Athletico Paranaense\").\n+if state:\n+    combo = f\"{key} {state.lower()}\"\n+    if combo in TEAM_ALIASES:\n+        return TEAM_ALIASES[combo]\n+# 3) Ambiguous bases must keep a geographic qualifier to stay distinct.\n if key in AMBIGUOUS_BASES:\n     if state:\n         return f\"{AMBIGUOUS_BASES[key]}-{state}\"\n     if country:\n","additions":7,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py","time":{"start":1788206110173,"end":1788206110175}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Very informative:\n1. Some BR-Foot rows have primary dates within 1 day (2015-11-20 vs 2015-11-19) — date shift (timezone or recording differences).\n2. Some pairs are missing entirely in primary 2015 (e.g., \"Santos x Atletico Paranaense\" 2015-12-06) — wait, primary has all 380 matches of 2015... unless \"Atletico Paranaense\" key differs. key_team(\"Atletico Paranaense\") → alias \"atletico paranaense\" → \"Athletico Paranaense\" → key \"athletico paranaense\". In primary, the team appears as \"Atletico-PR\" → canonical \"Athletico Paranaense\" → same key. Hmm, then why None? Unless 2015 primary actually doesn't contain Athletico-PR fixtures? 2015 Série A included Athletico-PR. Let me debug that specific pair.\n\nWait — actually let me recheck: maybe by_pair lookup key uses sorted tuple but I built by_pair with sorted keys too ✓. Let me check what primary names for Athletico Paranaense look like in 2015. Actually the earlier near-check found 'near': 62 for 2015 — with pairs existing. The 'none': 73. But this run shows pair=None for several. Possible cause: primary 2015 names use \"Atletico-PR\" → canonical... wait, canonical_team(\"Atletico-PR\"): base \"Atletico\", state \"PR\" → key \"atletico\" → alias dict has \"atletico pr\" but key here is bare \"atletico\" (state stripped before alias lookup!). Then `if key in AMBIGUOUS_BASES` — \"atletico\" IS in AMBIGUOUS_BASES → returns \"Atlético\" since no country... but state! I return `f\"{AMBIGUOUS_BASES[key]}-{state}\"` = \"Atlético-PR\" ONLY if state present. State \"PR\" was stripped → state=\"PR\" ✓ → returns \"Atlético-PR\". Key: \"atletico pr\" → NOT in TEAM_ALIASES as key→ wait \"atletico pr\" IS in TEAM_ALIASES (→ \"Athletico Paranaense\"). But AMBIGUOUS_BASES check happens FIRST and short-circuits with \"Atlético-PR\"!\n\nBug: alias lookup must happen before ambiguous-with-state fallback, or the alias check should also consider key+state combos. Fix order in canonical_team:\n1. key of base\n2. If key in TEAM_ALIASES → return alias. (For \"atletico\" + state PR, key \"atletico\" is not in TEAM_ALIASES, good.)\n3. elif key in AMBIGUOUS_BASES: with state → \"Atlético-PR\"? But desired canonical for \"Atletico-PR\" is \"Athletico Paranaense\". So combine: when base key ambiguous with state, look up alias on f\"{key} {state.lower()}\" first: \"atletico pr\" → in TEAM_ALIASES → \"Athletico Paranaense\" ✓. For \"america\" + \"MG\": \"america mg\" in TEAM_ALIASES → \"América Mineiro\" ✓. For \"nacional\" + \"AM\": \"nacional am\" → TEAM_ALIASES has \"nacional am\" → \"Nacional-AM\" ✓. For \"america\" + \"RN\": \"america rn\" → \"América-RN\" ✓. Fallback if combo not aliased: f\"{base}-{state}\".\n\nSo new order:\n```python\nkey = normalize_key(base)\nif key in TEAM_ALIASES: return TEAM_ALIASES[key]\ncombo = f\"{key} {state.lower()}\" if state else None\nif combo and combo in TEAM_ALIASES: return TEAM_ALIASES[combo]\nif key in AMBIGUOUS_BASES:\n    if state: return f\"{AMBIGUOUS_BASES[key]}-{state}\"\n    if country: return f\"{AMBIGUOUS_BASES[key]} ({country})\"\nif country: return f\"{base} ({country})\"\nreturn base\n```\n\nThis fixes \"Atletico-PR\" → \"Athletico Paranaense\", \"Atletico-MG\" → \"Atlético Mineiro\", \"Atletico-GO\" → \"Atlético Goianiense\", \"America-MG\" → \"América Mineiro\", etc. These were all broken → explains massive dedupe leakage and wrong team stats (two canonical names for the same club: \"Atlético-PR\" from brasileirao vs \"Athletico Paranaense\" from libertadores/BR-Foot).\n\nAlso \"Vasco Da Gama RJ\" → base \"Vasco Da Gama\" state RJ → key \"vasco da gama\" in aliases → \"Vasco da Gama\" ✓.\n\nAlso check \"Santos x Athletico Paranaense 2015-12-06\" — after fix, primary's \"Atletico-PR\" canonicalizes to \"Athletico Paranaense\" matching BR-Foot's \"Atletico Paranaense\" ✓.\n\nAlso add near-date dedupe (±3 days) as second-chance? The 11-19 vs 11-20 case: date recorded differently. For standings correctness, deduping those matters. Approach: exact-date dedupe first; then for extended-file rows (BR-Foot), check for a primary match same comp+season+pair within ±3 days. Risk: two legs of same pair within 3 days — vanishingly rare in league play (consecutive rounds are a week apart). For cup (two legs a week apart) same comp+pair within ±3 days could mismatch legs, but goals equal? Eh. I'll implement the ±3 day second pass ONLY for duplicates where team-pair+season+competition match and dates differ by 1-3 days. Cup legs are typically 7 days apart so ±3 won't wrongly merge them.\n\nLet me also double check Libertadores canonicals after fix: \"Atlético Nacional\" (Colombian) key \"atletico nacional\" — not aliased, not ambiguous → returns as-is ✓. \"Atlético-MG\" in Libertadores → \"Atlético Mineiro\" ✓ now consistent with BR-Foot \"Atletico Mineiro\" ✓ and fifa \"Atlético Mineiro\" ✓. \n\nNow also think: \"America-MG\" in brasileirao file → \"América Mineiro\"; in cup file \"América - MG\" → same ✓; BR-Foot \"America MG\" → same ✓.\n\nFix canonical_team now.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05963d5d2001gZ81DMC3hxQqnA","sessionID":"ses_fa6ae4622ffeRIXSVkVPYYmujp","messageID":"msg_0596326cd001jHPZI3XvtWAd7Z"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1788206110236,"sessionID":"ses_fa6ae4622ffeRIXSVkVPYYmujp","part":{"id":"prt_05963bea30013wEhwUq5ajAwSr","messageID":"msg_0596326cd001jHPZI3XvtWAd7Z","sessionID":"ses_fa6ae4622ffeRIXSVkVPYYmujp","type":"text","text":"Found a real bug: `canonical_team` checks `AMBIGUOUS_BASES` before trying `key + state` aliases, so \"Atletico-PR\" never became \"Athletico Paranaense\" — causing dedupe leakage. Fixing:","time":{"start":1788206104227,"end":1788206110233}}}
