ever triggers because the near key includes team keys!).\n\nWait — but some BR-Foot Fortaleza matches DID dedupe (Santos 2019-08-25 has \"Fortaleza FC\" merged into \"Santos 3-3 Fortaleza\"? No — look: \"2019-08-25 Santos 3-3 Fortaleza [Brasileirao]\" AND \"2019-08-25 Santos 3-3 Fortaleza FC [BR-Football]\" — NOT deduped. All Fortaleza pairs leak. That explains +38 Fortaleza-ish anomalies... 21 teams × 2 = 42 extra matches? 2019: 21 teams = 20 + phantom? No wait — count: 2019 had \"Fortaleza FC\" as 21st team with only some matches? The output shows teams with != 38: only some teams got listed... The counter showed over = teams with != 38 matches — I only saw a snippet. \"Fortaleza FC\" played BR-Foot-only matches (those not deduped) — since every Fortaleza fixture leaked, \"Fortaleza\" itself would have 38 and \"Fortaleza FC\" would have however many BR-Foot rows for 2019 Serie A exist (~38). Hmm, but Flamengo shows 40 (38 + 2 leaked Fortaleza matches).\n\nWait but why didn't the near-match dedupe catch \"2019-11-28 Fortaleza 2-1 Santos\" vs \"2019-11-28 Fortaleza FC 2-1 Santos\" — exact same date, different team key (\"fortaleza\" vs \"fortaleza fc\") → exact dedupe key differs (team keys differ) and near key differs too. The near-match logic keyed on team pairs can't help when names don't canonicalize the same.\n\nSo the fix: add \"fortaleza fc\" → Fortaleza alias. This also matters for team queries (\"Fortaleza FC\" is a very plausible user query!). Let me also scan ALL BR-Foot names that don't map into the primary team set to catch remaining variant gaps systematically, across all seasons and all tournaments.\n\nBetter: build a diagnostic that lists BR-Foot canonical keys not present in the union of all canonical team keys from primary files... but BR-Foot includes Serie B/C teams not in primary. Instead, fuzzy-check: for each BR-Foot key, is there a primary file key that overlaps suspiciously (like \"fortaleza\" ⊂ \"fortaleza fc\")? Actually simpler: manually review the list of BR-Foot canonical names (271 distinct) — print those ending with common suffixes or not in alias table. Let me print all distinct canonical names from BR-Foot that are not in TEAM_ALIASES values (i.e., fell through to raw base), and eyeball for split-identity problems (e.g. \"Fortaleza FC\").\n\nAlso cup file: \"Fortaleza Esporte Clube\"? aliased \"fortaleza esporte clube\" ✓. Let me run the diagnostic.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05965c6c2001NqxqG7bZ0UTatF","sessionID":"ses_fa6ae4622ffeRIXSVkVPYYmujp","messageID":"msg_059654e24001vGrBqXkSfUa9sv"}}
