gs clean ✓ (verified: 20 teams, Flamengo champion ✓).\n\nFor 2021, a pragmatic fix: within a (competition, season), if a team pair appears more than twice... complex. Alternative pragmatic fix: match-count sanity — for league standings, keep it as-is; the 2021 phantom teams each have 10-12 matches so they'd rank last — visually odd but explainable. Hmm.\n\nBetter engineering fix: prefer primary-file seasons. Rule: when loading BR-Football rows for a (competition, season) that a primary file already fully covers, dedupe harder — merge ANY same-pair match in that season that is within ±30 days? Risky.\n\nCleanest robust rule for league tables: for each (competition, season), count per-team matches; the standings query could restrict to teams with ≥ 2×median matches... no, too hacky.\n\nActually — let me look at those 44 stray rows more closely. If they're mislabeled \"Serie A\" (actually Serie B), the same (date, pair) might exist in primary's... there IS no Serie B in primary. Hmm. Let me look at a few rows: Botafogo's 10 \"Serie A\" 2021 matches in BR-Foot — dates and opponents. Botafogo 2021: played Serie B (champion, promoted). If the 10-12 matches are vs Serie B teams (Sport? no Sport played Serie A 2021)... The pairs listed include ('Flamengo', 'Sport Recife'): 3 — both real Serie A teams. And stray pairs like Botafogo x Coritiba? Let me check what those 4 teams' matches look like — opponents and dates.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0596bab03001xt7P7KxGb0p3MJ","sessionID":"ses_fa6ae4622ffeRIXSVkVPYYmujp","messageID":"msg_0596ad771001HyQajwvNCLRfO3"}}
