{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788206692455,"sessionID":"ses_fa6ae4622ffeRIXSVkVPYYmujp","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_7224c6e8786c44ff934a9d6d","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py","newString":"    @staticmethod\n    def _near_key(match: Match) -> tuple:\n        # Note: deliberately excludes season -- files that derive season from\n        # the match date mislabel end-of-season fixtures (e.g. the 2020\n        # Brasileirão finished in Feb 2021).  The +-3 day window keeps this\n        # safe from cross-leg merges (cup ties are a week apart).\n        comp = match.competition_key\n        home, away = sorted((key_team(match.home_team), key_team(match.away_team)))\n        return (comp, home, away)","oldString":"    @staticmethod\n    def _near_key(match: Match) -> tuple:\n        comp = match.competition_key\n        home, away = sorted((key_team(match.home_team), key_team(match.away_team)))\n        return (comp, match.season, home, away)"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n@@ -256,11 +256,15 @@\n         self.skipped[filename] = count\n \n @staticmethod\n def _near_key(match: Match) -> tuple:\n+    # Note: deliberately excludes season -- files that derive season from\n+    # the match date mislabel end-of-season fixtures (e.g. the 2020\n+    # Brasileirão finished in Feb 2021).  The +-3 day window keeps this\n+    # safe from cross-leg merges (cup ties are a week apart).\n     comp = match.competition_key\n     home, away = sorted((key_team(match.home_team), key_team(match.away_team)))\n-    return (comp, match.season, home, away)\n+    return (comp, home, away)\n \n @staticmethod\n def _find_near_match(match: Match, near_index: dict) -> Match | None:\n     if not match.date:\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n@@ -256,11 +256,15 @@\n         self.skipped[filename] = count\n \n @staticmethod\n def _near_key(match: Match) -> tuple:\n+    # Note: deliberately excludes season -- files that derive season from\n+    # the match date mislabel end-of-season fixtures (e.g. the 2020\n+    # Brasileirão finished in Feb 2021).  The +-3 day window keeps this\n+    # safe from cross-leg merges (cup ties are a week apart).\n     comp = match.competition_key\n     home, away = sorted((key_team(match.home_team), key_team(match.away_team)))\n-    return (comp, match.season, home, away)\n+    return (comp, home, away)\n \n @staticmethod\n def _find_near_match(match: Match, near_index: dict) -> Match | None:\n     if not match.date:\n","additions":5,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py","time":{"start":1788206692447,"end":1788206692453}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"\"2021-02-25 21:30 Ceara-CE 2-1 Botafogo-RJ [season 2020]\" vs BR-Foot \"2021-02-26 Ceara 2-1 Botafogo RJ\" — a **1-day date difference**! My near-dedupe should catch this (delta=1)... but it didn't!\n\nWhy? Order of file loading: Brasileirao_Matches loads first, indexes into near_index. BR-Foot processes later. For the BR-Foot row: exact key miss (date 02-26 vs 02-25 differ) → `_find_near_match` searches near_index for (comp, season, home_key, away_key) — **season!** The near key includes `match.season`: BR-Foot row season = 2021 (derived from date), primary row season = 2020. Near key mismatch → no candidate found!\n\nFix: make the near-match lookup season-agnostic for the near index, OR drop season from the near key. Since the near key is only used for within-season-ish fuzzy matching, dropping season entirely could merge two legs of a cup tie across season boundary — negligible. But there's the cup two-leg concern: two legs 7 days apart → delta=7 > 3 ✓ safe. Dropping season from near key is fine given the ±3 window.\n\nWait, but why did primary-only vs primary overlaps (novo vs brasileirao) work? Exact dates there. And some BR-Foot rows matched with near? Some did (Flamengo's 12 extra rows deduped — because Flamengo's 2020-tail matches: e.g. Flamengo match on 2021-01-24 primary vs BR-Foot 2021-01-24 same date → EXACT match (dedupe key has no season) ✓. So exact matches worked regardless of season; only the ±1-3 day shifted ones with cross-season derivation failed.\n\nAlso, \"2021-02-22 Botafogo 1-0 Sao Paulo [primary]\" vs BR-Foot \"2021-02-22 Botafogo RJ 1-0 Sao Paulo\" — exact same date → deduped ✓ (that's why Botafogo has only 10-12 strays, not all 12-13).\n\nFix: remove season from `_near_key`. Also \"4 de Julho EC\" vs \"4 de Julho\" alias. Let me also double check the near-match loop semantics: `0 < delta <= 3` — for exact-date we never get here. Within-file duplicates: BR-Foot rows processed sequentially; a later BR-Foot row with near date to an earlier BR-Foot row merges. But ordering: the 2021 file processed once — Flamengo x Sport x3 pairs (3 fixtures) — with 2 real (home/away) + 1 shifted-date dup → near-merge handles if ≤3 days.\n\nRisk of wrong-leg merging in cup: two legs typically 7+ days apart ✓.\n\nApply fix: `_near_key` drops season.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0596cb850001WYSJKLG0Uh0Qlr","sessionID":"ses_fa6ae4622ffeRIXSVkVPYYmujp","messageID":"msg_0596c4b32001x9K7v2lMabuZ6X"}}
