{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788206741486,"sessionID":"ses_fa6ae4622ffeRIXSVkVPYYmujp","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_d3baa96079e54e8aaa33f21c","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv\nfrom collections import Counter\nc = Counter()\nwith open('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv', encoding='utf-8-sig') as f:\n    for r in csv.DictReader(f): c[r['round']] += 1\nprint(dict(sorted(c.items(), key=lambda kv: (len(kv[0]), kv[0]))))\nEOF"},"output":"{'1': 334, '2': 376, '3': 258, '4': 140, '5': 123, '6': 62, '7': 30, '8': 14}\n","metadata":{"output":"{'1': 334, '2': 376, '3': 258, '4': 140, '5': 123, '6': 62, '7': 30, '8': 14}\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv\nfrom collections import Counter\nc = Counter()\nwith open('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv', encoding='utf-8-sig') as f:\n    for r in csv.DictReader(f): c[r['round']] += 1\nprint(dict(sorted(c.items(), key=lambda kv: (len(kv[0]), kv[0]))))\nEOF","time":{"start":1788206741479,"end":1788206741485}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"PERFECT! All four seasons now correct:\n- 2019: Flamengo ✓ (real champion)\n- 2020: Flamengo ✓ (real champion)\n- 2021: Atlético Mineiro ✓ (real champion)\n- 2022: Palmeiras ✓ (real champion)\n- All 20 teams × 38 matches ✓\n\nData layer is solid. Now let me write the tests: BDD feature files + step definitions + unit tests. Then verify the MCP server end-to-end (tool listing + calls + stdio).\n\nTest plan:\n\n**tests/conftest.py**: session-scoped `engine` fixture loading real data; `bdd_scenarios` helper.\n\n**features/*.feature** — five feature files covering the spec's BDD scenarios plus more:\n\n1. `match_queries.feature`:\n   - Find matches between two teams (Flamengo x Fluminense) → list with date/scores/competition\n   - Get matches for a team in a season\n   - Find Copa do Brasil finals (stage filter — cup rounds \"final\"? cup round values: let me check for \"final\" — cup round column values include numbers 1-6? I saw \"1\". Search \"final\" in round col. Libertadores has stage \"final\".)\n   - Filter by date range\n   - Unknown team returns graceful message\n\n2. `team_queries.feature`:\n   - Team statistics for Palmeiras 2023? — use 2022/2021 (in data). Spec example uses 2022. Corinthians home 2022.\n   - Win/loss/draw records incl. goals\n   - Compare Palmeiras and Santos head-to-head\n   - Team name variants resolve (Palmeiras-SP == Palmeiras)\n\n3. `player_queries.feature`:\n   - Find players by name (Neymar)\n   - Brazilian players\n   - Highest-rated players at a club (use a club in FIFA data, e.g. \"Grêmio\" or \"Real Madrid\")\n   - Player profile with attributes\n\n4. `competition_queries.feature`:\n   - 2019 Brasileirão champion = Flamengo 90 pts\n   - Relegated 2020\n   - Standings structure\n   - Unknown season → graceful\n\n5. `statistical_analysis.feature`:\n   - Average goals per match\n   - Home win rate < 100%\n   - Biggest wins sorted by margin\n   - Head-to-head record symmetry\n\n**Step definitions**: tests/steps/test_*.py using pytest-bdd `scenarios()` + given/when/then parsers. Given: \"the match data is loaded\" (fixture). When/Then with parsers like `when(parsers.parse('I search for matches between \"{team_a}\" and \"{team_b}\"'))`.\n\n**Unit tests**:\n- test_normalize.py: date formats, team variants table, parse_int.\n- test_data_loader.py: loads 6 files, row counts, dedupe sanity (2019 standings 20×38), unique match ids, player count, enrichment (arena, extra stats present).\n- test_knowledge_graph.py: node types present, neighbors, search.\n- test_server_tools.py: create_app(engine) → list_tools has 12 tools; call each tool via app.call_tool; results parse as JSON; error path works.\n\nLet me check cup \"final\" rounds quickly, then write all test files.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0596d77bb001s11GPqUGuVbt41","sessionID":"ses_fa6ae