\"Atletico\" + \"PR\" -> \"Athletico Paranaense\").\n if state:\n     combo = f\"{key} {state.lower()}\"\n     if combo in TEAM_ALIASES:\n         return TEAM_ALIASES[combo]\n-# 2b) State-dependent disambiguation with no alias entry.\n-if key == \"vitoria\" and state == \"ES\":\n-    return \"Vitória-ES\"\n # 3) Ambiguous bases must keep a geographic qualifier to stay distinct.\n if key in AMBIGUOUS_BASES:\n     if state:\n         return f\"{AMBIGUOUS_BASES[key]}-{state}\"\n","additions":4,"deletions":3},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py","time":{"start":1788207104224,"end":1788207104227}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"`canonical_team(\"Vitoria-BA\")` returns \"Vitoria\" (unaccented, no alias) — because raw input is unaccented \"Vitoria\" and there's no alias mapping \"vitoria\" → \"Vitória\" anymore (I removed it for the ES case). I need to restore the base alias but keep the ES override. Reorder logic: handle the state-dependent override BEFORE alias lookup. So:\n\n1. If state and key==\"vitoria\" and state==\"ES\" → \"Vitória-ES\"\n2. alias lookup (restore \"vitoria\": \"Vitória\")\n3. combo lookup\n4. ambiguous...\n\nSince rule 1 (ES) is more specific than the alias, put 2b before rule 1. Let me restructure: move the vitoria-ES check above the base-alias check.\n\nThen the other failures:\n- test_seasons_2012_to_2022_complete: some season ≠ 380. Which one? Probably 2021 or 2022 — near-dedupe might have OVER-merged now (near key drops season): a 2022 primary match vs a 2021 BR-Foot match with same pair within 3 days... e.g. season 2022 start (April 2022) vs season-2020-tail matches (Feb 2021)? No, too far. Within-file: cup? No — this is Serie A only. Let me see which season failed and how.\n- test_get_node_accent_insensitive: graph.get_node(\"sao paulo\") — search_nodes finds teams whose name contains \"sao paulo\"; team node name is \"São Paulo\" — `query in name_lower` → \"sao paulo\" not in \"são paulo\" (accent differs)! Node name search must fold accents. Fix KnowledgeGraph._by_name to index by folded key (unaccent+lower), and search/get_node to fold the query.\n- test_club_same_as_team: FIFA club \"Grêmio\" — SAME_AS edge created when club_key == team key. FIFA \"Grêmio\" → key_team(\"Grêmio\") = canonical → \"Grêmio\" ✓ team key \"gremio\" ✓ — should match... but graph.neighbors(\"Grêmio\") with edge_types SAME_AS — get_node(\"Grêmio\") might resolve to the TEAM node (exact name match, first in _by_name order?) rather than the CLUB node. Node \"Grêmio\" exists as both Team and Club (FIFA club name \"Grêmio\" identical!). get_node picks first id in _by_name[\"grêmio\"] — order depends on insertion: teams inserted before players/clubs → Team node first. So neighbors returns the Team node which has no SAME_AS edges. Fix the test to query the club explicitly... or better: make the test check the CLUB node — get_node returns Team; I should search node_types=[\"Club\"]. Update test to use graph.search_nodes(\"Grêmio\", node_types=[\"Club\"]) then neighbors of that node. Also the neighbors API could accept type filter — simpler to fix the test.\n\nAlso get_node accent folding fix will help \"sao paulo\".\n\nFor the season completeness failure, let me check which seasons/counts after fixing the others. Run and print counts.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0597300c3001fPwjVpKm22uLFX","sessionID":"ses_fa6ae4622ffeRIXSVkVPYYmujp","messageID":"msg_05972992d0016I0YS2jnrfM6yh"}}
