{"type":"text","timestamp":1788207255816,"sessionID":"ses_fa6ae4622ffeRIXSVkVPYYmujp","part":{"id":"prt_059753314001MrugnczfuKFplT","messageID":"msg_059745537001IwnkXFajwgz8Bp","sessionID":"ses_fa6ae4622ffeRIXSVkVPYYmujp","type":"text","text":"Two strays identified: a state-league row in BR-Foot (2016) and a scoreless postponed row vs a 14-days-later scored duplicate (2022). Fixing both with principled rules:","time":{"start":1788207248148,"end":1788207255814}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788207255827,"sessionID":"ses_fa6ae4622ffeRIXSVkVPYYmujp","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_3ef01dd1c78c44d8b833b73d","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py","newString":"    @staticmethod\n    def _find_near_match(match: Match, near_index: dict) -> Match | None:\n        if not match.date:\n            return None\n        target = date.fromisoformat(match.date)\n        best: Match | None = None\n        best_delta = 10**6\n        for candidate in near_index.get(SoccerData._near_key(match), []):\n            if not candidate.date:\n                continue\n            delta = abs((date.fromisoformat(candidate.date) - target).days)\n            if delta == 0 or delta > 30:\n                continue\n            # Tight window: any shifted-date duplicate.  Wide window: only\n            # merge scoreless placeholders (postponed fixtures recorded with\n            # NA scores) whose real result was filed under a later date.\n            if delta <= 3 or (candidate.home_goals is None and delta <= 30):\n                if delta < best_delta:\n                    best, best_delta = candidate, delta\n        return best","oldString":"    @staticmethod\n    def _find_near_match(match: Match, near_index: dict) -> Match | None:\n        if not match.date:\n            return None\n        target = date.fromisoformat(match.date)\n        for candidate in near_index.get(SoccerData._near_key(match), []):\n            if not candidate.date:\n                continue\n            delta = abs((date.fromisoformat(candidate.date) - target).days)\n            if 0 < delta <= 3:\n                return candidate\n        return None"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n@@ -269,15 +269,23 @@\n def _find_near_match(match: Match, near_index: dict) -> Match | None:\n     if not match.date:\n         return None\n     target = date.fromisoformat(match.date)\n+    best: Match | None = None\n+    best_delta = 10**6\n     for candidate in near_index.get(SoccerData._near_key(match), []):\n         if not candidate.date:\n             continue\n         delta = abs((date.fromisoformat(candidate.date) - target).days)\n-        if 0 < delta <= 3:\n-            return candidate\n-    return None\n+        if delta == 0 or delta > 30:\n+            continue\n+        # Tight window: any shifted-date duplicate.  Wide window: only\n+        # merge scoreless placeholders (postponed fixtures recorded with\n+        # NA scores) whose real result was filed under a later date.\n+        if delta <= 3 or (candidate.home_goals is None and delta <= 30):\n+            if delta < best_delta:\n+                best, best_delta = candidate, delta\n+    return best\n \n @staticmethod\n def _index_near(match: Match, near_index: dict) -> None:\n     if match.date:\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n@@ -269,15 +269,23 @@\n def _find_near_match(match: Match, near_index: dict) -> Match | None:\n     if not match.date:\n         return None\n     target = date.fromisoformat(match.date)\n+    best: Match | None = None\n+    best_delta = 10**6\n     for candidate in near_index.get(SoccerData._near_key(match), []):\n         if not candidate.date:\n             continue\n         delta = abs((date.fromisoformat(candidate.date) - target).days)\n-        if 0 < delta <= 3:\n-            return candidate\n-    return None\n+        if delta == 0 or delta > 30:\n+            continue\n+        # Tight window: any shifted-date duplicate.  Wide window: only\n+        # merge scoreless placeholders (postponed fixtures recorded with\n+        # NA scores) whose real result was filed under a later date.\n+        if delta <= 3 or (candidate.home_goals is None and delta <= 30):\n+            if delta < best_delta:\n+                best, best_delta = candidate, delta\n+    return best\n \n @staticmethod\n def _index_near(match: Match, near_index: dict) -> None:\n     if match.date:\n","additions":11,"deletions":3},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py","time":{"start":1788207255823,"end":1788207255825}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Two issues:\n\n1. **2016 \"Brasília x CA Taguatinga\"** — a Campeonato Brasiliense (state league) match mislabeled \"Serie A\" in BR-Football? Or mislabeled by my canonical_competition? BR-Foot tournament \"Serie A\" for that row... it's state-league junk in the file (Brasília and CA Taguatinga are Distrito Federal clubs, Jan 2016 = state league period). It leaked because no primary match exists. Handle: it's one stray row; not fixable via aliases. Options: leave it (minor noise) or filter. A principled filter: for Serie A, a match between two teams never seen in Serie A elsewhere... too clever. I'll leave it — it's genuine source noise (10,296-row file). It doesn't affect standings questions materially (2016: Palmeiras champion — the stray adds one match to 2 teams that aren't Serie A 2016 clubs; standings will show 22 teams though!). Hmm, that pollutes the 2016 standings (\"Show the 2016 table\" → 22 rows). Test test_seasons_2012_to_2022_complete asserts 380 per season — I wrote that test expecting perfection. Options:\n   a) Relax the test (380±1) — honest about source data noise.\n   b) Filter state-league strays: heuristic — a Serie A match where neither team appears in any other Serie A season match (with ≥ N matches)? Brasília/CA Taguatinga appear exactly once in the whole Serie A comp. Legit 2016 Serie A teams each appear 38 times. Rule: when loading BR-Foot rows, if the pair's teams have < 5 total matches in that competition... this heuristic could misfire for early cup rounds (Copa do Brasil small clubs have 1-2 matches each legitimately!). Only apply to league competitions (Série A/B/C) where every team plays ≥ 30 matches/season. Implementation: post-load cleanup pass per league competition: drop matches where EITHER team's total appearance count in that competition < 10. Risk: a legitimate 2020-tail match of a relegated team? Those teams have 38 appearances — safe. Série B/C: BR-Foot-only competition — all matches loaded fresh; teams have ~34-38 appearances... but 2023 Série B teams: BR-Foot covers 2014-2023 → full seasons, fine. Teams with <10: would drop partial junk. Edge: does BR-Foot Serie B have partial coverage years? Serie B count 3677 / 10 years ≈ 368/year ✓ full. Serie C 1807/10 ≈ 180/year — Série C has 20 teams × 38 = 760... no wait Série C format: ~20 teams, first phase fewer games. 180/year is way less — partial coverage! Serie C 1807 rows over 2014-2023 = ~180/year, but a real Série C season has ~552+ matches (20+ teams). So BR-Foot Série C coverage is partial (only some matches). Dropping teams with <10 appearances could nuke legit partial data. Apply the cleanup ONLY to Série A (the competition with complete primary coverage)? For Série A, every legit team has 38/season, and the strays (Brasília etc.) have 1-2. Safe.\n\n   Simpler + safer: apply cleanup pass only for \"Brasileirão Série A\": drop matches (from non-primary sources) where a team has fewer than 10 total appearances in Série A across the whole dataset. Legit teams across seasons accumulate ≥38; strays have 1-2.\n\n   Wait — but old-era 2003-2011 matches come from novo; those teams (Santo André, Barueri, Ipatinga...) have 38+ appearances ✓. Only truly stray rows get dropped.\n\n2. **2022 Corinthians x Goiás**: primary has \"2022-10-15 Goiás None-None Corinthians\" (NA scores — postponed match row!) and BR-Foot has \"2022-10-29 Goiás 0-0 Corinthians\". The actual match was played 2022-10-29 (or the BR-Foot date). Primary kept it (exact+near missed: 14 days apart) and BR-Foot added as separate. Result: 381 matches, one with None scores. Fix options: widen near-window to ±14 days? Risky for cup legs (7 days apart!). Alternative: second-chance dedupe for rows with NO SCORES: if an existing match has None goals and a new match has same pair+competition within ±30 days, merge (fill scores). That's principled: a scoreless row carries no result info; pairing it with the scored duplicate is safe. Implement in _find_near_match/_enrich flow: special-case when existing.home_goals is None → window ±30 days. And prefer keeping the scored one? Merging fills the None row with scores ✓ (enrich copies goals when keep has None).\n\nLet me implement both:\n- In `_find_near_match(match, near_index)`: two passes — first strict window (1-3 days), then if the candidate has unknown goals, window up to 30 days.\n  Actually invert: find candidates where delta <= 3, OR (candidate has None goals and delta <= 30). Wait direction: we're adding `match` (BR-Foot, scored 10-29); existing primary row (10-15, None goals). Merge into existing (earlier file) → enrich fills goals from duplicate ✓. So candidate (existing) has None goals → allow delta up to 30.\n- Post-load cleanup for Série A strays: after load(), for competition_key(\"Brasileirão Série A\"), compute team appearance counts; drop matches where min(appearances[home], appearances[away]) < 10 AND source is BR-Football (only drop extended-file strays; primary files are authoritative). Hmm — actually why limit to BR-Foot? A primary Serie A row with a team having <10 appearances would be... legitimate small sample? Primary Serie A is complete per season — every team has 38. Strays only come from BR-Foot. But what about a BR-Foot row of a REAL Serie A fixture that primary missed entirely (a match primary lacks)? Primary is exactly 380/season = complete; nothing missing. Safe.\n\nAlso note: those None-score rows in primary 2022 (postponed Oct/Nov 2022 with NA) — with the ±30-day scoreless merge, they'll get scores from BR-Foot where available. 2022 primary had 8 Botafogo None rows; BR-Foot has 2022 coverage 377 rows — most should merge now. Result: 2022 = 380 complete with scores.\n\nImplement both fixes.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_059755101001YA6haeOAFPdUIz","sessionID":"ses_fa6ae4622ffeRIXSVkVPYYmujp","messageID":"msg_059745537001IwnkXFajwgz8Bp"}}
