{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788207276550,"sessionID":"ses_fa6ae4622ffeRIXSVkVPYYmujp","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_7e6ab8b477ef460b868ab636","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py","newString":"        seen: dict[tuple, Match] = {}\n        near_index: dict[tuple, list[Match]] = {}\n        for filename in _MATCH_FILES:\n            self._load_match_file(filename, seen, near_index)\n        self._drop_league_strays()\n        self._load_player_file(_PLAYER_FILE)\n        self._build_indexes()\n\n    def _drop_league_strays(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Remove junk rows from league data (e.g. state-league matches\n        mislabeled \"Serie A\" in the extended-stats file).\n\n        A real Brasileirão Série A team accumulates dozens of appearances in\n        the dataset; stray fixtures involve teams seen only once or twice.\n        Only extended-file rows are ever dropped -- the dedicated match files\n        are authoritative.\n        \"\"\"\n        serie_a = competition_key(\"Brasileirão Série A\")\n        in_serie_a = [m for m in self.matches if m.competition_key == serie_a]\n        counts: dict[str, int] = {}\n        for m in in_serie_a:\n            for team in (m.home_team, m.away_team):\n                counts[key_team(team)] = counts.get(key_team(team), 0) + 1\n        strays = {\n            m.match_id\n            for m in in_serie_a\n            if m.source == \"BR-Football-Dataset.csv\" and min(\n                counts.get(key_team(m.home_team), 0),\n                counts.get(key_team(m.away_team), 0),\n            ) < _LEAGUE_MIN_APPEARANCES\n        }\n        if strays:\n            self.matches = [m for m in self.matches if m.match_id not in strays]","oldString":"        seen: dict[tuple, Match] = {}\n        near_index: dict[tuple, list[Match]] = {}\n        for filename in _MATCH_FILES:\n            self._load_match_file(filename, seen, near_index)\n        self._load_player_file(_PLAYER_FILE)\n        self._build_indexes()"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n@@ -221,11 +221,38 @@\n     seen: dict[tuple, Match] = {}\n     near_index: dict[tuple, list[Match]] = {}\n     for filename in _MATCH_FILES:\n         self._load_match_file(filename, seen, near_index)\n+    self._drop_league_strays()\n     self._load_player_file(_PLAYER_FILE)\n     self._build_indexes()\n \n+def _drop_league_strays(self) -> None:\n+    \"\"\"Remove junk rows from league data (e.g. state-league matches\n+    mislabeled \"Serie A\" in the extended-stats file).\n+\n+    A real Brasileirão Série A team accumulates dozens of appearances in\n+    the dataset; stray fixtures involve teams seen only once or twice.\n+    Only extended-file rows are ever dropped -- the dedicated match files\n+    are authoritative.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    serie_a = competition_key(\"Brasileirão Série A\")\n+    in_serie_a = [m for m in self.matches if m.competition_key == serie_a]\n+    counts: dict[str, int] = {}\n+    for m in in_serie_a:\n+        for team in (m.home_team, m.away_team):\n+            counts[key_team(team)] = counts.get(key_team(team), 0) + 1\n+    strays = {\n+        m.match_id\n+        for m in in_serie_a\n+        if m.source == \"BR-Football-Dataset.csv\" and min(\n+            counts.get(key_team(m.home_team), 0),\n+            counts.get(key_team(m.away_team), 0),\n+        ) < _LEAGUE_MIN_APPEARANCES\n+    }\n+    if strays:\n+        self.matches = [m for m in self.matches if m.match_id not in strays]\n+\n def _load_match_file(self, filename: str, seen: dict[tuple, Match],\n                      near_index: dict | None = None) -> None:\n     path = self.data_dir / filename\n     if not path.exists():\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n@@ -221,11 +221,38 @@\n     seen: dict[tuple, Match] = {}\n     near_index: dict[tuple, list[Match]] = {}\n     for filename in _MATCH_FILES:\n         self._load_match_file(filename, seen, near_index)\n+    self._drop_league_strays()\n     self._load_player_file(_PLAYER_FILE)\n     self._build_indexes()\n \n+def _drop_league_strays(self) -> None:\n+    \"\"\"Remove junk rows from league data (e.g. state-league matches\n+    mislabeled \"Serie A\" in the extended-stats file).\n+\n+    A real Brasileirão Série A team accumulates dozens of appearances in\n+    the dataset; stray fixtures involve teams seen only once or twice.\n+    Only extended-file rows are ever dropped -- the dedicated match files\n+    are authoritative.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    serie_a = competition_key(\"Brasileirão Série A\")\n+    in_serie_a = [m for m in self.matches if m.competition_key == serie_a]\n+    counts: dict[str, int] = {}\n+    for m in in_serie_a:\n+        for team in (m.home_team, m.away_team):\n+            counts[key_team(team)] = counts.get(key_team(team), 0) + 1\n+    strays = {\n+        m.match_id\n+        for m in in_serie_a\n+        if m.source == \"BR-Football-Dataset.csv\" and min(\n+            counts.get(key_team(m.home_team), 0),\n+            counts.get(key_team(m.away_team), 0),\n+        ) < _LEAGUE_MIN_APPEARANCES\n+    }\n+    if strays:\n+        self.matches = [m for m in self.matches if m.match_id not in strays]\n+\n def _load_match_file(self, filename: str, seen: dict[tuple, Match],\n                      near_index: dict | None = None) -> None:\n     path = self.data_dir / filename\n     if not path.exists():\n","additions":27,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py","time":{"start":1788207276545,"end":1788207276548}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Wait — there's a subtlety: the primary file is loaded FIRST. When BR-Foot processes its rows, the near_index holds primary matches. But the direction: primary scoreless row (existing, loaded earlier) + BR-Foot scored row (match, being added) → `_find_near_match(match)` finds `candidate` = primary scoreless row → merge: enrich(candidate, match) fills candidate's goals ✓.\n\nBut ALSO: what if the primary row is scored and BR-Foot's row is the scoreless one? enrich(keep=primary, dup=scoreless) → goals stay ✓ good.\n\nAnd what if both within same file? e.g. two BR-Foot rows same pair within 30 days, first scoreless, second scored → merge ✓ good. Both scored, 14 days apart → NOT merged (delta>3, both scored) ✓ correct (could be different fixtures... in a league they'd never play twice in 14 days, but cup could).\n\nNow the Serie A stray cleanup. Add after load() loop, before _build_indexes: a pass dropping BR-Foot rows in Série A where a team has < 10 total Série A appearances.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05975a1e9001lUg6ZLGVt5k7Jz","sessionID":"ses_fa6ae4622ffeRIXSVkVPYYmujp","messageID":"msg_0597552a7001SgsOWGnNcXaaOe"}}
