{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788207409595,"sessionID":"ses_fa6ae4622ffeRIXSVkVPYYmujp","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_186a3930077045a4887f867a","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/features/team_queries.feature","newString":"  Scenario: Get team statistics for a season\n    When I request statistics for \"Palmeiras\" in season \"2022\" in competition \"Brasileirão Série A\"\n    Then I should receive wins, losses, draws and goals\n    And the team should have played 38 matches\n\n  Scenario: Team statistics with home venue split\n    When I request statistics for \"Corinthians\" in season \"2022\" in competition \"Brasileirão Série A\" at venue \"home\"\n    Then I should receive wins, losses, draws and goals\n    And the team should have played 19 matches","oldString":"  Scenario: Get team statistics for a season\n    When I request statistics for \"Palmeiras\" in season \"2022\"\n    Then I should receive wins, losses, draws and goals\n    And the team should have played 38 matches\n\n  Scenario: Team statistics with home venue split\n    When I request statistics for \"Corinthians\" in season \"2022\" at venue \"home\"\n    Then I should receive wins, losses, draws and goals\n    And the team should have played 19 matches"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/features/team_queries.feature\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/features/team_queries.feature\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/features/team_queries.feature\n@@ -6,14 +6,14 @@\n Background:\n   Given the Brazilian soccer data is loaded\n \n Scenario: Get team statistics for a season\n-  When I request statistics for \"Palmeiras\" in season \"2022\"\n+  When I request statistics for \"Palmeiras\" in season \"2022\" in competition \"Brasileirão Série A\"\n   Then I should receive wins, losses, draws and goals\n   And the team should have played 38 matches\n \n Scenario: Team statistics with home venue split\n-  When I request statistics for \"Corinthians\" in season \"2022\" at venue \"home\"\n+  When I request statistics for \"Corinthians\" in season \"2022\" in competition \"Brasileirão Série A\" at venue \"home\"\n   Then I should receive wins, losses, draws and goals\n   And the team should have played 19 matches\n \n Scenario: Team name variations are normalized\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/features/team_queries.feature","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/features/team_queries.feature\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/features/team_queries.feature\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/features/team_queries.feature\n@@ -6,14 +6,14 @@\n Background:\n   Given the Brazilian soccer data is loaded\n \n Scenario: Get team statistics for a season\n-  When I request statistics for \"Palmeiras\" in season \"2022\"\n+  When I request statistics for \"Palmeiras\" in season \"2022\" in competition \"Brasileirão Série A\"\n   Then I should receive wins, losses, draws and goals\n   And the team should have played 38 matches\n \n Scenario: Team statistics with home venue split\n-  When I request statistics for \"Corinthians\" in season \"2022\" at venue \"home\"\n+  When I request statistics for \"Corinthians\" in season \"2022\" in competition \"Brasileirão Série A\" at venue \"home\"\n   Then I should receive wins, losses, draws and goals\n   And the team should have played 19 matches\n \n Scenario: Team name variations are normalized\n","additions":2,"deletions":2},"truncated":false},"title":"features/team_queries.feature","time":{"start":1788207409587,"end":1788207409591}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Three distinct failures:\n\n1. **Palmeiras 2022 statistics: 54 played instead of 38** — Palmeiras 2022: Série A (38) + Copa do Brasil matches (13 in 2022: they won the cup) + Libertadores? team_statistics without competition filter includes ALL competitions → 38 + 13 cup + 3 lib? = 54. That's by design (\"all matches in dataset\" scope). My BDD scenario \"Get team statistics for a season / played 38\" assumed competition=Série A. Fix: the scenario should scope to the league: change When to 'I request statistics for \"Palmeiras\" in season \"2022\"' — expected behavior per TASK example (\"Corinthians home record (2022 Brasileirão)\") includes competition. I'll make the scenario explicitly scope to \"Brasileirão Série A\" — add competition param to the When step. Update feature + steps.\n\n2. **Libertadores stage \"final\"** — search_matches with stage=\"final\" matches \"semifinals\" because my stage filter is substring-based (\"final\" in \"semifinals\" ✓). Fix: stage filter should be exact (fold equality) OR match whole word. I'll use exact fold match, falling back to substring ONLY if no exact matches? Simpler: exact match on fold. \"group stage\" exact ✓, \"final\" exact ✓. Substring risks (semifinals) → use exact. But partial user input \"semi\"? Compromise: exact match first; if zero results, try substring. Implement in search_matches: two-pass.\n\n3. **test_server_tools async tests fail** — TestToolContract uses `async def test_...` without anyio/pytest-asyncio plugin → skipped? The failure output isn't shown. They're async tests: pytest will warn/skip \"async def functions are not natively supported\". The non-async call_tool tests presumably fail on team_statistics (Palmeiras 2019=38? No — test_team_statistics: Santos 2019 played == 38 ✓ ... the failing one is `test_team_statistics`? Output says TestToolCalls::test_team_statistics failed — Santos season 2019 → includes cup+libertadores → ≠38. Same scope issue: Santos 2019: Serie A 38 + Libertadores (Santos played lib 2019? yes finalist ~13) + cup. So expected ≠ 38. Fix test: scope competition \"Brasileirão Série A\" → 38. Or assert played >= 30. I'll scope it.\n\nFor the async tests: pytest without asyncio plugin collects async functions and errors. Install pytest-asyncio? Or make tests sync using asyncio.run inside. Simplest: make them sync and use asyncio.run(app.list_tools()). The call_tool helper already does asyncio.run. Let me convert TestToolContract to sync.\n\nFix the stage filter (exact-first) in queries.search_matches:\n```python\nif stage:\n    stage_fold = _fold(stage)\n    exact = [m for m in pool if m.stage and _fold(m.stage) == stage_fold]\n    if not exact:\n        exact = [m for m in pool if m.stage and stage_fold in _fold(m.stage)]\n    pool = exact\n```\n\nUpdate BDD team feature: \n```\nScenario: Get team statistics for a season\n    When I request statistics for \"Palmeiras\" in season \"2022\" in competition \"Brasileirão Série A\"\n    Then I should receive wins, losses, draws and goals\n    And the team should have played 38 matches\n```\nAnd venue scenario similarly with competition. Update steps accordingly. Also home venue: Corinthians home 2022 Série A = 19 ✓.\n\nAlso player scenario \"Brazilian players\" — fine. And team_statistics tests in test_server_tools: scope with competition.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05977a99b001WI9ojI8JQ5HmST","sessionID":"ses_fa6ae4622ffeRIXSVkVPYYmujp","messageID":"msg_0597741e9001XLVC7KFMMcxdQH"}}
