{"type":"text","timestamp":1788207621094,"sessionID":"ses_fa6ae4622ffeRIXSVkVPYYmujp","part":{"id":"prt_0597acf82001tOF2fbrLnpx036","messageID":"msg_0597a3fd8001wUiMfej4LGqyAX","sessionID":"ses_fa6ae4622ffeRIXSVkVPYYmujp","type":"text","text":"`resolve_team`'s fuzzy fallback is too loose (\"Maranhão\" ⊂ \"Atlético do Maranhão FC\"). Tightening with a generic-word rule:","time":{"start":1788207615874,"end":1788207621093}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788207621101,"sessionID":"ses_fa6ae4622ffeRIXSVkVPYYmujp","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_1e08940b34064d6fb683c4a6","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py","newString":"    def resolve_team(self, name: str) -> str | None:\n        \"\"\"Resolve a (possibly partial) team name to a canonical team name.\"\"\"\n        if not name:\n            return None\n        query = key_team(name)\n        if query in self._team_names:\n            return self._team_names[query]\n        # User typed a partial team name (\"palmei\" -> \"Palmeiras\").\n        for key, display in self._team_names.items():\n            if query and query in key:\n                return display\n        # User typed a team name with generic club qualifiers\n        # (\"Flamengo FC\" -> \"Flamengo\") -- but not extra distinct words.\n        stripped = \" \".join(\n            token for token in query.split() if token not in _GENERIC_CLUB_WORDS\n        )\n        if stripped and stripped != query and stripped in self._team_names:\n            return self._team_names[stripped]\n        return None","oldString":"    def resolve_team(self, name: str) -> str | None:\n        \"\"\"Resolve a (possibly partial) team name to a canonical team name.\"\"\"\n        if not name:\n            return None\n        query = key_team(name)\n        if query in self._team_names:\n            return self._team_names[query]\n        for key, display in self._team_names.items():\n            if query and (query in key or key in query):\n                return display\n        return None"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n@@ -548,11 +548,19 @@\n         return None\n     query = key_team(name)\n     if query in self._team_names:\n         return self._team_names[query]\n+    # User typed a partial team name (\"palmei\" -> \"Palmeiras\").\n     for key, display in self._team_names.items():\n-        if query and (query in key or key in query):\n+        if query and query in key:\n             return display\n+    # User typed a team name with generic club qualifiers\n+    # (\"Flamengo FC\" -> \"Flamengo\") -- but not extra distinct words.\n+    stripped = \" \".join(\n+        token for token in query.split() if token not in _GENERIC_CLUB_WORDS\n+    )\n+    if stripped and stripped != query and stripped in self._team_names:\n+        return self._team_names[stripped]\n     return None\n \n def team_names(self) -> list[str]:\n     \"\"\"Sorted canonical team names present in the match data.\"\"\"\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-7439bfc38313/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n@@ -548,11 +548,19 @@\n         return None\n     query = key_team(name)\n     if query in self._team_names:\n         return self._team_names[query]\n+    # User typed a partial team name (\"palmei\" -> \"Palmeiras\").\n     for key, display in self._team_names.items():\n-        if query and (query in key or key in query):\n+        if query and query in key:\n             return display\n+    # User typed a team name with generic club qualifiers\n+    # (\"Flamengo FC\" -> \"Flamengo\") -- but not extra distinct words.\n+    stripped = \" \".join(\n+        token for token in query.split() if token not in _GENERIC_CLUB_WORDS\n+    )\n+    if stripped and stripped != query and stripped in self._team_names:\n+        return self._team_names[stripped]\n     return None\n \n def team_names(self) -> list[str]:\n     \"\"\"Sorted canonical team names present in the match data.\"\"\"\n","additions":9,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py","time":{"start":1788207621097,"end":1788207621099}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"\"Atlético do Maranhão FC\" resolved to \"Maranhão\" via `resolve_team`'s fuzzy containment match (\"maranhão\" ⊂ \"atletico do maranhao fc\"... wait, resolve_team(\"Atlético do Maranhão FC\"): query = key = \"atletico do maranhao fc\" — no exact; fuzzy: for each known team key, `query in key or key in query` — team \"Maranhão\" key \"maranhao\" ⊂ query → match! The fuzzy matching is too loose for multiword queries with unknown club names.\n\nImprove resolve_team: for fuzzy fallback, require the query to be a SINGLE token (word) contained in a team key, or exact key match. For multi-token unknown queries, only allow substring matching when the QUERY is contained in a team key (e.g. \"fla\" → Flamengo? \"fla\" not in \"flamengo\"... it is: \"flamengo\".contains(\"fla\") ✓). The problem case is `key in query` for partial team names like \"maranhao\" in \"atletico do maranhao fc\" — that's the \"team name with extra words\" case which is useful (\"Flamengo\" query for \"Clube de Regatas do Flamengo\"? no — reverse: query has MORE words than team). Hmm, that direction exists for user queries like \"Clube de Regatas do Flamengo\" (query ⊃ key \"flamengo\").\n\nBetter heuristic: allow `key in query` only when the team key is a substantial word (len ≥ 5) AND all other query tokens are generic club words (fc, clube, esporte, ec, sc, do, da, de, do, the...)? That's getting complex. Pragmatic: strip generic club words from the query before matching: \"atletico do maranhao fc\" → tokens {atletico, maranhao} — \"atletico\" is not generic... still matches Maranhão via \"maranhao\" ⊂ query.\n\nAlternative: prefer EXACT token match: after stripping generic words, does any known team key EQUAL the remaining string? \"atletico maranhao\" ≠ \"maranhao\". Then substring `key in query` requires len(key) ≥ 6? \"maranhao\" is 8 — still passes. Hmm.\n\nHonestly the deepest issue: \"Atlético do Maranhão FC\" is a fictional unknown club in my test. Real-world semantics: this SHOULD probably match nothing since \"Atlético\" + \"Maranhão\" as a compound isn't in data. My fuzzy layer treats tokens independently.\n\nCleaner rule: fuzzy match only when EITHER (a) query ⊆ key (user typed partial team name: \"palmei\" ⊂ \"palmeiras\") — always allowed; OR (b) key ⊆ query AND the query tokens minus generic words are ALL covered... can't guarantee.\n\nSimplest robust: allow (b) only if query, after removing generic club-word tokens, equals exactly the key... no wait that's the exact case.\n\nLet me reconsider: when is `key in query` needed? User asks about \"Vasco da Gama-RJ\"? That canonicalizes through aliases. \"Clube de Regatas Vasco\"? query key \"clube de regatas vasco\" ⊃ \"vasco da gama\"? No — \"vasco da gama\" ⊄ \"clube de regatas vasco\". Hmm. \"Sport Club do Recife\" handled by aliases. Realistic case: query = canonical + extra qualifiers, e.g. \"Grêmio FBPA\" alias ✓. \"Flamengo FC\"? query \"flamengo fc\" ⊃ \"flamengo\" → match ✓ desirable.\n\nTrade-off: \"Flamengo FC\" desirable vs \"Atlético do Maranhão FC\" undesirable. Both multi-token superset queries. Distinguishing: in \"flamengo fc\", the extra token is a generic word. In \"atletico do maranhao fc\", after removing generic words {fc, do}, remains {atletico, maranhao} — the team key \"maranhao\" doesn't cover \"atletico\". Rule: after removing generic club words (fc, clube, club, esporte, ec, sc, do, da, de, dos, das, the, o, a) from query, the remainder must EQUAL the key for the `key ⊆ query` direction. \"flamengo fc\" → \"flamengo\" == \"flamengo\" ✓. \"atletico do maranhao fc\" → \"atletico maranhao\" ≠ \"maranhao\" ✗ (no match, correct). \"clube de regatas do flamengo\" → \"clube regatas flamengo\" ≠ \"flamengo\" ✗ — miss, but alias table covers variants; acceptable.\n\nAnd direction (a) query ⊆ key stays unrestricted (prefix/partial typing).\n\nImplement in SoccerData.resolve_team:\n```python\ndef resolve_team(self, name):\n    if not name: return None\n    query = key_team(name)\n    if query in self._team_names: return self._team_names[query]\n    # partial team name typed by the user (\"palmei\" -> Palmeiras)\n    for key, display in self._team_names.items():\n        if query and query in key:\n            return display\n    # team name with generic qualifiers (\"Flamengo FC\" -> Flamengo)\n    stripped = _strip_generic(query)\n    if stripped != query and stripped in self._team_names:\n        return self._team_names[stripped]\n    return None\n```\nGeneric words: {\"fc\",\"clube\",\"club\",\"esporte\",\"esportes\",\"ec\",\"sc\",\"futebol\",\"regatas\",\"do\",\"da\",\"de\",\"dos\",\"das\",\"the\",\"atletico\"?} — careful: \"atletico\" is NOT generic (Atlético Mineiro etc. rely on it). Keep the list minimal: fc, clube, club, esporte, ec, sc, futebol, regatas, do, da, de, dos, das, the. \n\nWait but the test team \"Atlético do Maranhão FC\" → strip → \"atletico maranhao\" — not a key → None ✓.\n\nAlso \"sport\" query → exact key \"sport\" ✓ alias.\n\nEdge: does any BDD/unit test rely on `key in query` fuzzy? test_resolve_team_partial_names uses \"Palmeiras\"/\"Flamengo\" exact ✓. search_matches with partial? tests use full names ✓.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0597ae3dd001EYEKmCAGnH8Bow","sessionID":"ses_fa6ae4622ffeRIXSVkVPYYmujp","messageID":"msg_0597a3fd8001wUiMfej4LGqyAX"}}
