{"type":"text","timestamp":1788207879539,"sessionID":"ses_fa6ae4622ffeRIXSVkVPYYmujp","part":{"id":"prt_0597eb56400160Ay8vdpJSjp4E","messageID":"msg_0597e7507001wSCaV1Lxlu8O1D","sessionID":"ses_fa6ae4622ffeRIXSVkVPYYmujp","type":"text","text":"All 135 tests pass. Implementation complete:\n\n## Summary\n\nBuilt a **Brazilian Soccer MCP Server** in Python per TASK.md:\n\n**Package** (`brazilian_soccer_mcp/`)\n- `normalize.py` — team-name canonicalization (~200 aliases: state suffixes, accents, club prefixes, the three *Atleticos*, América-MG/RN, Nacional-AM vs Nacional-Uruguay), multi-format date parsing (ISO, ISO+time, DD/MM/YYYY)\n- `data_loader.py` — loads all 6 Kaggle CSVs (10,296 + 4,180 + 1,337 + 1,255 + 6,886 match rows + 18,207 players), dedupes overlapping fixtures across files with enrichment (arena, corners/shots/attacks), indexes by team/pair/competition-season\n- `knowledge_graph.py` — in-memory property graph: Team/Player/Club/Competition/Match nodes; PLAYED, BEAT, DREW_WITH, PLAYS_FOR, PARTICIPATES_IN, SAME_AS edges\n- `queries.py` + `server.py` — 12 MCP tools (official `mcp` SDK, stdio): match search, head-to-head, team stats/comparison/overview, standings, competition stats, biggest wins, player search/profile, graph search/neighbors\n\n**Verified against reality**: 2019 Brasileirão standings = Flamengo 90 pts (28W 6D 4L) with correct relegations — matches the spec's example answer; every season 2012–2022 computes a complete 20×38 table; champions 2003–2022 all correct.\n\n**Tests**: 135 passing — pytest-bdd Gherkin scenarios (`features/`, 5 features covering the spec's BDD cases) + unit tests for normalization/dedupe/graph + end-to-end MCP tool calls, plus a live JSON-RPC stdio smoke test (initialize → tools/list → tools/call).\n\nRun with `venv/bin/python -m brazilian_soccer_mcp` or `venv/bin/python -m pytest` for the suite.","time":{"start":1788207871332,"end":1788207879535}}}
